\begin{abstract}
This academic manuscript presents the mathematical foundations, computational 
architecture, stability envelope, and deterministic validation protocol of a 
real-time astrophysical refraction engine. The system integrates GPU-accelerated 
eikonal solvers, sparse voxel octrees, multi-wavelength dispersion sampling, and 
a Closed-Loop Deterministic Invariant Verifier (CL-DIV). CL-DIV enforces 
bitwise determinism, numerical stability, and cryptographically auditable 
correctness across all hardware layers.
