\section{Introduction}

Astrophysical refraction phenomena require modeling multi-index propagation 
through gravitational, plasma, and exotic media. Traditional approaches rely on 
offline computation due to the complexity of the eikonal equation and the 
computational cost of multi-wavelength ray integration. This work introduces a 
real-time architecture capable of resolving chromatic anomalies across 
$280$--$1900$ nm while maintaining deterministic correctness.

\section{Mathematical Framework}

The engine solves the scalar eikonal equation:
\[
|\nabla \Phi| = n(\mathbf{x}),
\]
where $\Phi$ is the optical path function and $n(\mathbf{x})$ is the effective 
refractive index:
\[
n_{\text{eff}}(r,\lambda) = n_g(r) + n_p(\lambda) + n_{\text{exo}}(r,\lambda).
\]

Ray propagation is computed via RK4 integration:
\[
\mathbf{x}'(s) = \frac{1}{n_{\text{eff}}} \nabla \Phi.
\]

